# WordPress PHP Conventions (ANM)

See `edminboost-anm-compliance.mdc` for the security gate.

## File Header

Every PHP file must start with:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Brief description.
 *
 * @package EdminBoost\AdminNoticeManager
 */

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}
```

`uninstall.php` uses `WP_UNINSTALL_PLUGIN` instead of `ABSPATH`.

## Security

- Check capabilities before rendering admin pages: `current_user_can( EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::CAPABILITY )` on site admin; `current_user_can( EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::NETWORK_CAPABILITY )` on network admin screens.
- Escape output: `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_html_e()`.
- Sanitize site settings via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize()` as `sanitize_callback` in `register_setting()`; network defaults via `sanitize_network_settings()`; network policy via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::sanitize_policy()`.
- New AJAX handlers: register in `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ajax::register_hooks()`, implement `handle_*`, call `verify_request()` (honor posted `context` for network vs site); use `verify_site_settings_mutation()` when changing site-level settings storage (digest/webhook preview: sanitize nested input with dedicated helpers when accepting unsaved form fields).

## WordPress APIs

- Register hooks in `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Plugin::run()` or class `register_hooks()` — not in the bootstrap file (except activation/deactivation registration).
- Use Settings API for the main settings option (`register_setting`, `settings_fields`, `submit_button`). Rules/inbox use dedicated classes + AJAX where appropriate.
- Enqueue assets with `EDMINBOOST_ANM_VERSION` as the version string.
- Pass data to JS via `wp_localize_script()` — global `edminboostAnmData` from `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::get_localized_data()`.
- Page slugs: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` with `-inbox`, `-rules`, `-settings`, `-billing` suffixes.
- Inbox list: sanitize GET/POST list args via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::parse_inbox_list_args()`; paginate with `get_inbox_list_slice()` (20 per page). `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Inbox::query()` honors `page` / `per_page` after filtering.

## Class Wiring

- Bootstrap requires core classes; instantiate only via `edminboost_anm_run_plugin()`.
- `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Plugin` constructor: `Admin`, `Notices`, `Interceptor`, `Ajax`, `Digest`, `Ad_Redirects`.
- Domain helpers (static or instantiated as needed): `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Rules`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Inbox`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Stats`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Importer`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Webhook`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ad_Redirects` (URL normalize/match helpers), `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite` (network policy, merge layers, uninstall network-wide).
- Bootstrap requires `class-edminboost-anm-multisite.php` (always loaded). Activation seeds options via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Activator` (+ network sitemeta when network-activated); deactivation clears digest schedule; `wp_initialize_site` seeds new blogs via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Plugin::handle_new_site()`.

## Settings Option Shape (top-level keys)

```php
array(
	'enabled'                              => false,
	'hide_core_notices'                    => false,
	'manage_notices_mode'                  => 'hide_selected', // show_all | hide_all | hide_selected | compact_panel
	'disable_plugin_update_notifications'  => false,
	'disable_core_update_notifications'    => false,
	'standard_admin_notices'               => array( /* per-level handling */ ),
	'non_standard_admin_notices'           => array(
		'no_level'             => 'inbox',
		'css_ignore_selectors' => '',
	),
	'hiding_notifications'                 => array( 'mode' => 'all', 'users' => array() ),
	'acl'                                  => array( 'roles' => array() ),
	'notice_panel'                         => array(
		'enabled'     => true,
		'style'       => 'link',       // link | bell_link | dropdown | dropdown_compact
		'position'    => 'default',    // see get_notice_panel_position_slugs()
		'badge_style' => 'count',      // count | count_9plus | count_99plus | dot | dot_pulse | none
		'colors'      => array( /* badge, badge_text, accent, accent_hover, bell_active */ ),
	),
	'upsell_preset'     => array( 'enabled' => false, 'custom_phrases' => array() ),
	'safety_guard'      => array( 'enabled' => true, 'mode' => 'strict' ),
	'client_shield'     => array( 'enabled' => false, 'roles' => array( ... ) ),
	'digest'            => array(
		'enabled'                => false,
		'recipients'             => 'admin@...',
		'send_weekday'           => 'monday',  // EDMINBOOST_ANM_Digest::DEFAULT_SEND_WEEKDAY; see get_send_weekday_choices()
		'subject'                => '',  // empty = default; supports {site_name}
		'intro'                  => '',
		'include_stats'          => true,
		'include_recent_notices' => true,
		'recent_notices_count'   => 10,  // clamped 1–25 in sanitize
		'footer'                 => '',
	),
	'webhook'           => array(
		'enabled' => false,
		'url'     => '',
		'message' => '',  // empty = default template; token placeholders in EDMINBOOST_ANM_Webhook
	),
	'word_filters'      => array( 'spam_words' => array(), 'whitelist_words' => array() ),
	'block_ad_redirects'=> array( 'enabled' => false, 'urls' => array() ),
	'white_label'       => array(
		'enabled'        => false,
		'menu_title'     => '',
		'brand_name'     => '',
		'logo_url'       => '',
		'hide_docs_link' => false,
		'docs_url'       => '',
		'hide_brand'     => false,
	),
)
```

Separate per-site options: `RULES_OPTION` (rule list), `INBOX_OPTION` (captured notices), `STATS_OPTION` (counters). Multisite sitemeta: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::NETWORK_OPTION`, `NETWORK_SETTINGS_OPTION`, `NETWORK_RULES_OPTION`.

## Partials

| Partial | Context |
|---------|---------|
| `edminboost-anm-dashboard-page.php` | Dashboard stats + quick actions |
| `edminboost-anm-inbox-page.php` | Inbox list table shell |
| `edminboost-anm-inbox-table-rows.php` | Inbox `<tr>` fragment (page + AJAX) |
| `edminboost-anm-rules-page.php` | Rules + WP preset conversion |
| `edminboost-anm-settings-page.php` | Settings API form (site or network defaults) |
| `edminboost-anm-network-policy-page.php` | Network multisite policy |
| `edminboost-anm-multisite-policy-fields.php` | Shared multisite policy fields fragment |
| `edminboost-anm-multisite-policy-next-steps.php` | Shared multisite policy next-steps links |
| `edminboost-anm-billing-page.php` | Billing / Free vs Pro comparison (read-only) |
| `edminboost-anm-notice-panel-dropdown.php` | Admin bar dropdown preview |

`EDMINBOOST_ANM_Notices::DROPDOWN_PREVIEW_LIMIT` (8) caps dropdown preview items.

- Settings help tips: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::help_tip( $message, $placement = 'below' )` — escaped dashicons + `data-tip` + `data-tip-placement` (`below`|`left`) for JS popup; output is safe HTML (escape in helper, document phpcs ignore when echoing in partials).
- Settings sanitize: `enabled` updated only when present in `$input` (Dashboard AJAX / explicit posts); other fields unchanged on Settings save.
- Display experience: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::DISPLAY_EXPERIENCE_PRESETS`, `get_display_experience_presets()`, `get_display_experience_preset_for_mode()`, `get_manage_notices_mode_labels()` — presets map to stored `manage_notices_mode`.
- Notice panel save: `sanitize()` sets `notice_panel.enabled` to true (no Settings UI toggle); `should_show_admin_bar_notice_panel()` checks plugin enabled + stored `notice_panel.enabled`.
- Notice panel: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::get_notice_panel_*()` registries; `get_notice_panel_admin_bar_placement()`, `get_notice_panel_preview_layout()` (default position → `left`), `notice_panel_position_uses_left_admin_bar()`, `notice_panel_style_is_dropdown()`, `notice_panel_style_uses_bell()`, `format_notice_panel_badge_display_count()`, etc. `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Notices::build_notice_badge_markup()` mirrors badge rules for live admin bar; `enqueue_admin_bar_dropdown_script()` shared for wp-admin and front-end admin bar dropdown JS; `get_plugin_screen_notice_hide_css()` + `hide_notices_on_plugin_screens()` for plugin-page notice clutter (exceptions for settings preview mocks).
- Inbox: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Inbox::snooze()` / `unsnooze()`, `is_actively_snoozed()`, `get_snooze_duration_key()`, `mark_read()`.
- Settings sanitize: update `upsell_preset` and `word_filters` only when present in `$input` (other tabs omit those keys).
- Webhook save: `sanitize_webhook_settings( $input, $stored )` merges with stored webhook; keeps URL when disabled or when a posted URL is invalid; `sanitize_webhook_url()` restricts endpoints to http/https.
- Admin routing: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::is_plugin_screen( $hook_suffix )` — screen id, optional hook suffix, or `$_GET['page']` contains `PAGE_SLUG`.
- Billing: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::get_billing_comparison_rows()`, `render_billing_comparison_cell()`, `get_billing_page_url()`; filter `edminboost_anm_billing_comparison`. Bootstrap defines `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PRO_URL` for upgrade links (user-initiated external navigation only).
- Digest: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Digest::build_email_content()`, `format_email_body_plain()`, `build_email()`, `get_preview()` (structured `content`, plain `body`, `next_send`), `get_recipients()`, `SITE_NAME_TOKEN`, `add_cron_schedules()`, `sync_schedule()`, `sanitize_send_weekday()`, `get_next_send_timestamp()`; filter `edminboost_anm_digest_email`.
- Rules: `save()` allows `match_type` `keyword`|`regex`|`css`; `html_matches_css_selector()`, `get_custom_blacklist_phrases()`, `get_active_blacklist_phrases()`; `context` `site`|`network` for storage; `get_all()` merges network rules when multisite sharing is enabled.
- Multisite: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::get_policy()`, `site_can_edit_settings()`, `site_can_edit_rules()`, `shares_network_rules()`, `merge_settings_layers()`, `is_network_plugin_screen()`.
- White label: `sanitize_white_label_settings()`, `is_white_label_enabled()`, menu/brand/docs URL helpers on `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings`.
- Webhook: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Webhook::build_payload()`, `build_message_text()`, `get_preview()`, `get_preview_notice()`, `get_sample_notice()`; filter `edminboost_anm_webhook_payload`.
- Sanitize helpers: `sanitize_digest_settings( $input, $stored )`, `sanitize_digest_recipients()`, `sanitize_webhook_settings( $input, $stored )`, `sanitize_webhook_url()` — Settings API `sanitize()` passes current `$output['digest']` / `$output['webhook']` as `$stored`; digest preview AJAX uses full digest sanitizer with stored merge; webhook preview AJAX uses `sanitize_webhook_settings()` with partial POST (message only in typical UI).

- Document `@var` annotations at the top of partials.
- Prefix partial-local variables with `$edminboost_anm_` to avoid collisions.

## Docblocks

Document all public methods with `@param`, `@return`, and `@var` on class properties.
